{%- comment -%}
  Seasonal product ribbon.

  Content lives in the admin, design lives here — the same split as `packshot`.
  A product earns the ribbon by being IN A COLLECTION, not by carrying a tag:
  the owner's rule is "every product in the ראש השנה collection", and membership is
  the thing he actually manages. A tag would be a second list to keep in sync,
  and the day it drifts from the collection is the day the wrong product wears
  a holiday badge.

  Both the collection it watches and the words it shows are theme settings, so
  the ribbon can be retargeted at the next holiday without touching Liquid.

  Accepts:
    product — the product object (required)

  Usage:
    {% render 'florista-ribbon', product: product %}

  Must be placed inside a positioned box — `.fc-media`, `.fp-media`, `.bs-link`.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # No `| default:` here, deliberately. Liquid's default filter treats an
  # EMPTY STRING as falsy, so `settings.ribbon_label | default: 'ראש השנה'`
  # puts the label back the moment the owner clears the field — and clearing it is
  # exactly how the schema says to switch the ribbon off after the holiday.
  # Shopify already falls back to the schema defaults when a setting has never
  # been saved, so the filter bought nothing and broke the off-switch.
  assign ribbon_collection = settings.ribbon_collection
  assign ribbon_label = settings.ribbon_label

  assign show_ribbon = false
  if ribbon_label != blank and ribbon_collection != blank
    for c in product.collections
      if c.handle == ribbon_collection
        assign show_ribbon = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_ribbon -%}
  <span class="florista-ribbon">{{ ribbon_label }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
